WEBVTT

1
01:00:00.966 --> 01:00:03.033
This single guide has more possible paths

2
01:00:03.166 --> 01:00:05.933
than Wikipedia has pages.

3
01:00:06.099 --> 01:00:06.699
But to the reader,

4
01:00:06.866 --> 01:00:08.833
it is just prose.

5
01:00:09.000 --> 01:00:11.099
Watch.

6
01:00:11.266 --> 01:00:12.033
Two readers.

7
01:00:12.199 --> 01:00:13.599
Two different paths.

8
01:00:13.766 --> 01:00:15.900
The guide adapts.

9
01:00:16.066 --> 01:00:16.599
Here,

10
01:00:16.766 --> 01:00:18.233
both paths merge.

11
01:00:18.400 --> 01:00:19.366
The same source.

12
01:00:19.533 --> 01:00:20.099
Referenced,

13
01:00:20.266 --> 01:00:21.566
not copied.

14
01:00:21.733 --> 01:00:22.933
In a linear document,

15
01:00:23.099 --> 01:00:25.000
this would be two guides to maintain.

16
01:00:25.166 --> 01:00:25.633
Here,

17
01:00:25.766 --> 01:00:27.400
it is one source.

18
01:00:27.566 --> 01:00:29.133
The paths diverge again.

19
01:00:29.300 --> 01:00:30.300
Different effort.

20
01:00:30.466 --> 01:00:32.099
Same tower.  

21
01:00:32.266 --> 01:00:37.066
And merge.

22
01:00:37.233 --> 01:00:38.300
Same crops.

23
01:00:38.500 --> 01:00:39.733
Different paths.

24
01:00:39.900 --> 01:00:40.699
One edit.

25
01:00:40.866 --> 01:00:43.766
Every branch updated.

26
01:00:43.933 --> 01:00:49.400
The detail is there.

27
01:00:49.566 --> 01:00:51.466
But not in the way.

28
01:00:52.766 --> 01:00:54.466
Complex, branching knowledge.

29
01:00:54.633 --> 01:00:56.566
Maintained like a single document.

30
01:00:56.733 --> 01:00:57.699
Delivered like prose.

